  "content": {
    "id": "p27-q13",
    "type": "question",
    "label": "13",
    "prompt": "Consider the dataset: $10, 8, 3, 2, 5, p$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-a",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "a",
        "prompt": "What value of $p$ would make the mean of this dataset 6?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-a-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p=8",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The six values must total $6\\times6=36$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10+8+3+2+5&=28\\\\p&=36-28\\\\p&=8\\end{align*}$$",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 24
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-b",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "b",
        "prompt": "What value of $p$ would make the median of this dataset 6?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-b-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p=7",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The known values in ascending order are $2,3,5,8,10$. To give a median of 6, $p$ must lie between 5 and 8, so the middle values are $5$ and $p$.\n\n$$\\begin{align*}\\frac{5+p}{2}&=6\\\\5+p&=12\\\\p&=7\\end{align*}$$\n\nThe sorted list is $2,3,5,7,8,10$; its median is $\\frac{5+7}{2}=6$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 32
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-c",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "c",
        "prompt": "What value of $p$ would make the mode of this dataset 8?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-c-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p=8",
                    "display": false
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "Each known value occurs once. With $p=8$, 8 occurs twice and every other value occurs once, so the mode is 8.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 10
      },
      {
        "id": "p27-q13-d",
        "type": "part",
        "label": "d",
        "prompt": "What value of $p$ would make the range of this dataset 11?",
        "layout": "list",
        "columns": null,
        "questionDiagrams": [],
        "children": [],
        "answer": {
          "short": {
            "format": "maths-editor-document-v1",
            "version": 1,
            "blocks": [
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-d-supplied-answer",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p=-1",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " or ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "p=13",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              },
              {
                "id": "p27-q13-d-short-method",
                "type": "paragraph",
                "fontSize": null,
                "align": "left",
                "spaceBefore": 0,
                "spaceAfter": 2,
                "lineHeight": 1.4,
                "indent": 0,
                "inlines": [
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "10-(-1)=11",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": " and ",
                    "marks": []
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "math",
                    "latex": "13-2=11",
                    "display": false
                  },
                  {
                    "type": "text",
                    "text": ".",
                    "marks": []
                  }
                ]
              }
            ]
          },
          "worked": "The known minimum is 2 and maximum is 10. Range is maximum minus minimum.\n\nIf $p$ is the new maximum:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}p-2&=11\\\\p&=13\\end{align*}$$\n\nIf $p$ is the new minimum:\n\n$$\\begin{align*}10-p&=11\\\\p&=-1\\end{align*}$$\n\nA value from 2 to 10 leaves the range at 8. Therefore $p=-1$ or $p=13$.",
          "solutionDiagrams": []
        },
        "answerSpaceMm": 36
      }
    ]
